{
  "id": 309832425,
  "iid": 16065,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Fix array bounds in conversation_new_deinterlaced().",
  "description": "GCC's static analysis (with assistance from `__attribute__((alloc_size(n)))`\nannotations) reports a trivial buffer overrun writing beyond the end of the\n`new_key` array.  Fix the array bounds to account for the fact that the array\nwill end with an element for the \"anchor\" followed by the actual terminating\n`CE_CONVERSATION_TYPE` element.\n\n(I plan to add `__attribute__((alloc_size(n)))` to a few functions, by means of the `G_GNUC_ALLOC_SIZE(n)` macro, in a follow-up change.)",
  "state": "merged",
